# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# staging/ = scratch (multi-GB total): derived response matrices, supplement
# extractions (~600MB), k-fold param dumps, ad-hoc fitters, per-run console
# logs, and the big fitted-item CSV. None of it is a deliverable and it is all
# regenerable from runs. The shareable CAT + calibration deliverables (figures,
# summary tables, metrics, manifest) are copied into reports/ (tracked).
#
# Written as `staging/**` + a directory re-include rather than a bare `staging/`
# so the small fit manifests below can be negated: git will not descend into an
# excluded DIRECTORY, so `staging/` would make any negation a silent no-op.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
staging/**
!staging/**/

# Exception: the fit audit trail (~60KB each). These carry the exact argv, the
# response-matrix sha256, EM convergence, the AIC/BIC model comparison and the
# latent correlation matrix -- the evidence behind the dimensionality decisions,
# which is not reconstructable from the calibrated banks alone.
!staging/**/*_manifest.json
!staging/**/coverage_report.json

# ...but not the judge-shard wrappers, which are run plumbing rather than
# calibration provenance.
staging/supp_v2/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Heavy / generated artifacts, depth-agnostic: raw model-output dumps, judge
# run-data, binary matrices, and all archives. These live in S3 or are
# regenerable, and are never tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tutorbench-responses*/
tutorbench-grading*/
grading/
run_data*.jsonl
run_data*.csv
*.npy
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# Calibration handoff / supplement bundles (tens-to-hundreds of MB).
qwen_calibration_handoff_32k_20260728/
handoff_extract/
supplement_handoff_build/
supplement_v2/

# Bridge raw judged matrix (raw grading output from S3/ORCD; regenerable, never tracked).
bridgegrade/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated plots (the curated set lives in plots/)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tutorbench_tb33_grading/
!plots/*.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data: the benchmark dataset IS tracked (needed on every machine that runs the
# pipeline); ignore only ad-hoc/derived jsonl dropped at the data/ root. This
# glob is single-level, so per-benchmark subdirs like data/TutorBench/ and
# data/IFEval/ are tracked automatically.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/*.jsonl

# Throwaway A/B experiment banks (regenerable; conclusions live in the memos,
# the authoritative bank is data/TutorBench/curated/).
data/TutorBench/experimental/
data/experimental/

# EduBench: candidate-bank scenario/rubric artifacts (HF-derived, reproducible
# via scripts/ingest_edubench.py / scripts/build_edubench_merged.py) -- never
# tracked, regardless of nesting depth (unmerged/, merged/, given_qmat/, ...).
data/EduBench/**/scenarios.json
data/EduBench/**/scenarios.jsonl
data/EduBench/**/rubrics.json
data/EduBench/**/rubrics.jsonl
# Raw HF en_data/*.jsonl source (~90MB incl. model_predictions, reproducible).
data/EduBench/en_data/

# Dr. SCI: large HF-derived parquet + generated scenario/rubric/CSV artifacts
# (multiple GBs; jsonl regenerable via scripts/build_dr_sci_scenarios.py).
data/dr-sci/*.parquet
data/dr-sci/*.jsonl
data/dr-sci/*.csv

# TutorEval processing intermediates: only the finalized bank
# (*_final.{jsonl,json}) and the human-reviewed edit sheet (reframe_review.tsv)
# are tracked. The clean / coverage / reframed / sample / verification stage
# files are deterministically regenerable scratch (~6MB each) and stay local.
data/TutorEval/*_clean.json
data/TutorEval/*_clean.jsonl
data/TutorEval/*_coverage.json
data/TutorEval/*_coverage.jsonl
data/TutorEval/*_reframed.json
data/TutorEval/*_reframed.jsonl
data/TutorEval/*_sample.json
data/TutorEval/*_sample.jsonl
data/TutorEval/*.sample*.json
data/TutorEval/*.sample*.jsonl
data/TutorEval/rubrics_qmatrix.json
data/TutorEval/rubrics_qmatrix.jsonl
data/TutorEval/rubrics_qmatrix.smoke.jsonl
data/TutorEval/rubrics_qmatrix_verified.json
data/TutorEval/rubrics_qmatrix_verified.jsonl
data/TutorEval/review_queue.jsonl
data/TutorEval/review_queue*.tsv
WildBenchGrade/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# reports/ = TRACKED deliverables (CAT figures + summary tables). The global
# *.png rule above (and any other broad ignore) must NOT swallow these, so
# re-include the whole reports/ tree explicitly. Keep this block LAST.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!reports/
!reports/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# regenerated_figures/ = TRACKED reproductions of the CAT recovery + pIRT
# figures on a dense quadrature grid (continuous ability axis), produced by
# scripts/regen_cat_figures.py. Same rationale as reports/: re-include past the
# global *.png rule.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!regenerated_figures/
!regenerated_figures/**


# Criteria-rewording run artifacts: per-item logs are regenerable and stay local
# (consistent with the qmatrix_logs handling). The reworded scenario copy (~6MB) is
# regenerable via scripts/build_final_rubrics.py --reword-sheet; only the human-reviewed
# sheets (wording_flags.tsv, wording_review.tsv) and the reworded rubric bank are tracked.
reword_logs/
data/TutorEval/scenarios_reworded.json
data/TutorEval/scenarios_reworded.jsonl

# cached BiGGen released-judgments pull (scripts/biggen_*_probe/structure)
biggen_results_cache.parquet

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# api_judge_pilot/ = frontier API-judge pilot. TRACK the deliverables: the
# harness/tooling scripts, docs, human labels, the finalized judge checkpoints
# (frozen prompt/config/metrics + reference verdicts), the human-labeled gold
# sets (*_core), and the biggen response-matrix. IGNORE the heavy regenerable
# scratch: the ~22MB raw verdicts.jsonl, every prompt-sweep / diagnostic /
# smoke results dir, and the big scenario/rubric source dumps.
#
# Written as `**` + a directory re-include (not a bare `api_judge_pilot/`) so
# the negations below take effect -- git will not descend into a bare excluded
# directory, which would silently no-op every `!` rule.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
api_judge_pilot/**
!api_judge_pilot/**/

# Scripts, docs, and the human label set.
!api_judge_pilot/*.py
!api_judge_pilot/*.md
!api_judge_pilot/gold/*.py
!api_judge_pilot/gold/*.md
!api_judge_pilot/human_labels.csv

# Finalized judge checkpoints (frozen provenance; small).
!api_judge_pilot/checkpoints/**

# Human-labeled gold sets: labels + sampled packets + manifests.
!api_judge_pilot/gold/biggen_core/**
!api_judge_pilot/gold/tutoreval_core/**
!api_judge_pilot/gold/tutorbench_core/**
!api_judge_pilot/gold/tutoreval_src/**

# The biggen response-matrix deliverable (models x criteria pass/fail + index).
!api_judge_pilot/grading_biggen/response_matrix.csv
!api_judge_pilot/grading_biggen/criteria_index.csv
!api_judge_pilot/grading_biggen/summary.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Branch-local experimental grid reports for tutorbench / tutoreval: untracked
# scratch (oos/stop grids, of_record builds, figures, __pycache__) that is
# regenerable and not a deliverable on this branch. Placed AFTER the reports/
# re-include above so these win (last match); no negations follow, so git skips
# these directories entirely.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
reports/*tutorbench*/
reports/*tutoreval*/
reports/*infobench*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BiGGen gemini-3 recalibration (branch frq/biggen) packaging.
#
# reports/biggen_gemini3_recal/ is SCRATCH: every shareable deliverable (the
# curated gemini-3 bank, the of-record figures/metrics, the OOS floor x SE grid
# + DECISION_TABLE, the SE_judge tables, and the repro scripts) was copied into
# the TRACKED biggen_calibration/ package. Ignore the scratch source so
# `git add -A` does not stage the duplicate multi-MB banks (biggen_unidim_
# modeled_gemini3*.jsonl), the engine dump (_bank_engine.jsonl), or __pycache__.
# Placed after the reports/ re-include above so it wins (last match).
#
# The large raw api_judge_pilot dumps (grading_*/verdicts.jsonl 23-91MB,
# biggen_src/ + *_src scenario/rubric dumps) are ALREADY excluded by the
# `api_judge_pilot/**` base rule above; the small provenance we shipped lives
# under biggen_calibration/bank/ (a copy) and is unaffected. NOTE: the
# api_judge_pilot/checkpoints/*.jsonl and gold/*_core files are SMALL frozen
# human-gold / reference deliverables (all < 200KB except the ~1MB core sample
# dumps) that the base rule intentionally re-includes -- left tracked on purpose.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
reports/biggen_gemini3_recal/

# Cross-branch leftover raw grading dumps (regenerable from S3/runs; never
# tracked). Most are already ignored above; these harden it if they reappear.
WildBenchGrade/
bridgegrade/
TutorEvalGrade/
api_judge_pilot/grading_*/verdicts.jsonl

# Guarantee the biggen_calibration/ package figures stay TRACKED (no broad *.png
# ignore currently swallows them; make it explicit + future-proof). Keep LAST.
!biggen_calibration/**/*.png
